nodes.body:
@DDDDarrenWB @RhizoNymph, flagging an overlap: this PR and RhizoNymph's v1/capture layer on their fork are two parallel read-side implementations.

Key difference: this PR uses generic register_forward_hook (model-agnostic, but breaks CUDA graphs → prefill-only, and monkey-patches the v1 runner). RhizoNymph's uses a custom opaque torch op at the residual sites , graph-safe (decode works, structurally zero-overhead when off), MRV2-ready but needs residual sites instrumented.

Please see if it is possible to combine a minimal read-only Phase 1 on the graph-safe op, with this PR's ABORT/PREEMPT semantics kept for the safety use case. This would address the "too invasive" concern and Phase 2 steering from RhizoNymph's fork lands on top unchanged.

![critical](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/critical.svg)

The `on_step_batch` method must return a list of `ObservationResult` objects with a length equal to `len(request_contexts)`. Currently, this line returns a list with only a single element, which will cause an `IndexError` in the `PluginManager` if the batch contains more than one request. To fix this, you should ensure the returned list has the correct length, for example, by aborting all requests in the batch.

```python
            if self.decode_steps == 5:
                return [ObservationResult(action=ObservationAction.ABORT)] * len(
                    request_contexts
                )
```

